# STACKIT Landing Zone Accelerator: **${platform_identifier}**

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Organization** | `${organization_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${organization_url})) |
| **Root Folder** | `${root_folder_name}`, `${root_folder_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${root_folder_url})) |
| **Management Project** | `${management_project_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${management_project_url})) |
| **meshStack Platform** | ${display_name} (`${platform_identifier}`) |
| **Building Block Definition** | ${display_name} |
| **STACKIT Project Service Account** | `${service_account_email}` |

## Network Areas

%{ if length(network_areas) == 0 ~}
The export has no connectivity, so the run created no network area.
%{ else ~}
The run created the hub and spoke networking of the export.

| Area | Network Area |
|------|--------------|
%{ for area, id in network_areas ~}
| `${area}` | `${id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](https://portal.stackit.cloud/network-area/network-areas/${id}/overview?organization=${organization_id})) |
%{ endfor ~}
%{ endif ~}

## Landing Zones

%{ if length(landing_zones) == 0 ~}
The export has no landing zones, so the platform has none either.
%{ else ~}
| Landing Zone | Identifier | Folder |
|--------------|------------|--------|
%{ for name, lz in landing_zones ~}
| ${lz.display_name} | `${name}` | `${lz.folder}` |
%{ endfor ~}
%{ endif ~}

## Order a STACKIT Project

Create an environment (a project with one tenant) and pick:

1. **Platform:** ${display_name}
2. **Landing zone:** one from the table above. The project is created in its folder.
3. **Building block:** ${display_name}. It asks for no inputs.

%{ if length(landing_zone_tags) > 0 ~}
The landing zones carry the tags below. meshStack offers a landing zone only when the project's
tags fit its tag policies, so choose project tag values from this list:

| Landing Zone Tag | Values |
|------------------|--------|
%{ for tag in landing_zone_tags ~}
| `${tag.key}` | ${join(", ", [for v in tag.values : "`${v}`"])} |
%{ endfor ~}
%{ endif ~}

%{ if playground_mode }
> **Playground mode.** The platform identifier carries a random suffix so this deployment does not
> occupy a name for good. Publish this platform or the STACKIT Project definition to other
> workspaces only to test that path, and delete the playground afterwards.
%{ endif ~}
